\ Spitfire: Edinburgh and Glasgow, and the whole scenery's assembly. Each
\ landmark stands at its Wikidata position. Published heights are used
\ where found: the castle rock 80 m above its surroundings, the Great Hall
\ 29 m by 12.5 m, the Half Moon Battery's wall 80 ft on its south side, the
\ six-storey New Barracks, St Giles' crown spire 44 m and the church 60 m by
\ 38 m, the Hub's spire 73 m, the Tron Kirk 52 m, the Balmoral Hotel 52 m,
\ the Scott Monument 61 m, the Nelson Monument 32 m, the National
\ Monument's twelve columns, St Mary's Cathedral 90 m, Fettes College 60 m;
\ in Glasgow the University's tower 85 m and its south front 160 m, the
\ Cathedral 87 m by 20 m, 32 m to its ridge and 69 m to its spire's tip,
\ the City Chambers' tower 73 m, Kelvingrove's roof 36 m and towers 51 m,
\ Trinity College's west tower over 50 m with two smaller ones east of it,
\ the Finnieston Crane 53 m and the Titan at Clydebank 46 m. The castle's
\ plan (where each building stands on the rock), the buildings' footprints
\ where no figure was found, and the National Monument's column height are
\ estimates.

\ a landmark's point on the ground beneath it, hills included
: on-ground ( key -- point )
	| key |
	key landmark-ground to point
	[ point first point first point 2 @i ground-height point 2 @i ] ;

\ === the cities' streets, squares, stations and railways, from OpenStreetMap ===

0x8a7a6a constant rail-colour
0xc8745c constant sandstone-colour
0x8fbf70 constant park-colour

\ tenements along a street's centre line, a block's height high, a row of blocks on the given sides of every stretch long enough for one; the sides :north for the north side alone, where gardens face the street
: keep-street-line ( line height sides -- )
	| line height sides |
	0 line size 1- 1 do k
		line k @i to start
		line k 1+ @i to finish
		[ finish first start first - 0 finish second start second - ] to run
		run heading-of to heading
		sides :north = if
			heading PI 180 / * sin 0 > if [ -1 ] else [ 1 ] then
		else
			sides
		then to row-sides
		run v-length 102 / round-down to n-blocks
		n-blocks 0 > if
			[ start first 0 start second ] heading n-blocks 90 12 height row-sides keep-street
		then
	loop ;

\ a street's line begun where it first passes a distance from a point, for a street that starts inside a landmark's grounds
: line-beyond ( line point distance -- line' )
	| line point distance |
	line first to start
	line second to finish
	0 101 1 do k
		start finish k 100 / v-between to probe
		probe point v- spread to dz to dx
		dx sq dz sq + sqrt distance >= if
			[ probe ] line 1 skip concat exit
		then
	loop
	line 1 skip ;

\ a square: its outline and the paths across it corner to corner
: keep-square ( outline -- )
	| outline |
	new-sketch to square
	square outline 0 ground-path sketch-loop
	outline size 2 / round-down to half
	square [ outline first outline half @i ] 0 ground-path sketch-path
	square [ outline second outline half 1+ outline size mod @i ] 0 ground-path sketch-path
	square park-colour keep ;

\ a city's OpenStreetMap features: tenements along its streets, each street's height and sides from styles keyed like the streets; its squares; its stations' train sheds, each its height from shed-heights; its railways on the ground, each run of track once
: keep-city ( streets styles squares stations shed-heights railways -- )
	| streets styles squares stations shed-heights railways |
	streets keys ( key | streets key @ styles key @ spread keep-street-line ) each
	squares values ( outline | outline keep-square ) each
	new-sketch to sheds
	stations keys ( key | sheds stations key @ 0 ground-path shed-heights key @ sketch-prism ) each
	sheds stone-colour keep
	railways ( line | line 1 ground-path rail-colour keep-path ) each ;

\ the middle of an outline, the mean of its points
: outline-middle ( outline -- point )
	| outline |
	outline [ 0 0 ] ' v+ reduce outline size 1 swap / v* ;

\ === Edinburgh Castle ===

\ the rock's top above the town, metres
78 constant castle-rock

\ the castle rock: its top, a ledge 40% of the way up and close in under the top, so the crags above it stand nearly sheer over the slope to the foot; the curtain wall round the top
: build-castle-rock ( -- )
	[ [ -95 25 ] [ -80 -15 ] [ -45 -38 ] [ 10 -35 ] [ 60 -30 ] [ 100 -15 ] [ 125 0 ]
	  [ 125 35 ] [ 95 62 ] [ 40 85 ] [ -20 84 ] [ -70 70 ] [ -95 48 ] ] to top
	[ [ -175 30 ] [ -155 -55 ] [ -85 -115 ] [ 10 -115 ] [ 85 -105 ] [ 150 -60 ] [ 190 -15 ]
	  [ 190 55 ] [ 140 120 ] [ 45 155 ] [ -40 155 ] [ -125 135 ] [ -175 85 ] ] to foot
	top size to n-points
	[ 0 n-points 1 do k
		top k @i to upper
		foot k @i to lower
		[ upper first 0.88 * lower first 0.12 * + upper second 0.88 * lower second 0.12 * + ]
	loop ] to ledge
	new-sketch to rock
	rock top castle-rock outline-at sketch-points to top-indices
	rock ledge castle-rock 0.4 * outline-at sketch-points to ledge-indices
	rock foot 0 outline-at sketch-points to foot-indices
	rock top-indices join-loop
	rock ledge-indices join-loop
	rock foot-indices join-loop
	0 n-points 1 do k
		rock [ top-indices k @i ledge-indices k @i foot-indices k @i ] join-path
	loop
	rock hill-colour keep
	new-sketch to wall
	wall top castle-rock outline-at 8 sketch-prism
	wall stone-colour keep ;

\ the castle's buildings about Crown Square, the batteries and gates to the east, the barracks to the south-west, the esplanade and Castlehill running down to the Royal Mile
: build-castle-buildings ( -- )
	site-heading to heading
	new-sketch to castle
	castle 0 0 castle-rock at heading 6 11 5 8 sketch-house
	castle 19 25 castle-rock at heading 14 40 13 19 sketch-house
	castle 19 14 castle-rock at heading 10 10 16 sketch-box
	castle [ [ 4 33 ] [ 34 33 ] [ 34 63 ] [ 4 63 ] ] castle-rock 0.2 + outline-at sketch-loop
	castle 19 70 castle-rock at heading 12.5 29 12 18 sketch-house
	castle 47 48 castle-rock at heading 90 + 14 40 18 24 sketch-house
	castle 47 26 castle-rock at heading 8 8 30 sketch-box
	castle 47 26 castle-rock at 8 30 36 4 sketch-pinnacled-spire
	castle -10 48 castle-rock at heading 90 + 12 36 12 17 sketch-house
	castle -40 30 castle-rock at heading 12 20 12 17 sketch-house
	castle -75 40 castle-rock at heading 90 + 12 30 12 16 sketch-house
	castle -45 70 castle-rock 8 - at heading 16 60 30 sketch-box
	[ -90 -60 -30 0 30 60 90 ] ( angle |
		angle PI 180 / * to bearing
		[ 78 bearing cos 24 * + 45 bearing sin 24 * + ]
	) map to battery
	castle battery castle-rock 22 - outline-at 28 sketch-prism
	castle 95 18 castle-rock 10 - at heading 12 10 22 sketch-box
	castle 130 18 castle-rock 6 - at heading 22 10 14 sketch-box
	[ -9 9 ] ( side | castle 130 18 side + castle-rock 6 - at heading 4 4 18 sketch-box ) each
	castle [ [ 135 -5 ] [ 230 -5 ] [ 230 45 ] [ 135 45 ] ] castle-rock 4 - outline-at sketch-loop
	castle [ 230 -5 castle-rock 12 - at 420 0 0 at ] sketch-path
	castle [ 230 45 castle-rock 12 - at 420 40 0 at ] sketch-path
	castle stone-colour keep ;

: build-castle ( -- )
	:st-margarets-chapel landmark-ground :edinburgh-castle :holyrood landmark-heading site!
	build-castle-rock
	build-castle-buildings ;

